   "published": "Tue, 24 Nov 2026 06:47:03 GMT",
   "_dt": 1795502823.0,
   "ageDays": 0.01,
   "summary": "Exports by small and midsized enterprises (SMEs) accounted for nearly 24 percent of Korea's total outbound shipments in the first 10 months of the year as the country's exports surpassed $1 trillion for the first time, customs data showed Tuesday. Korean SMEs exported $222.3 billion worth of goods in the January-October period, accounting for 23.9 percent of the country's total exports of $930.2 billion, according to data from the Korea Customs Service.",
   "summary_zh": "韩国关税厅周二公布的数据显示，随着该国出口额首次突破1万亿美元，今年前10个月，中小企业的出口占韩国出口总额的近24%。据韩国关税厅数据，1月至10月，韩国中小企业出口了价值2223亿美元的商品，占该国9302亿美元出口总额的23.9%。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Exports by small and midsized enterprises (SMEs) accounted for nearly 24 percent of Korea's total outbound shipments in the first 10 months of the year as the country's exports surpassed $1 trillion for the first time, customs data showed Tuesday. Korean SMEs exported $222.3 billion worth of goods in the January-October period, accounting for 23.9 percent of the country's total exports of $930.2 billion, according to data from the Korea Customs Service. The figure represents a 35.1 percent increase from $164.5 billion recorded in the same period of 2011, when the country first achieved $500 billion in annual exports. After nearly 15 years, Korea's annual exports surpassed the $1 trillion mark Thursday, making it the fourth country in the world to achieve the milestone after the United States, Germany and China. The number of exporting SMEs rose 22.2 percent to 96,286 in the January-October period of 2026 compared with the same period 15 years earlier. Nearly 300 SMEs exported $100 million or more worth of goods during the 10-month period, the customs data showed",
