   "title": "Nepal PM Balendra Shah arrives in Delhi for first official visit to India",
   "url": "https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/nepal-pm-balendra-shah-arrives-in-delhi-for-first-official-visit-to-india/article71731829.ece",
   "domain": "thehindu.com",
   "source": "thehindu.com",
   "published": "Sun, 22 Nov 2026 23:39:02 +0530",
   "_dt": 1795370942.0,
   "ageDays": 1.54,
   "summary": "Unlock these with Subscription The Prime Minister of Nepal, Balendra Shah, arrived in New Delhi on Sunday (November 22, 2026) afternoon for his first official visit to India. After the meeting, Mr. Jaishankar said, “Privileged to call on PM Balen Shah of Nepal on his visit to New Delhi this evening. Earlier on Sunday (November 22, 2026), Mr. Shah left Kathmandu on a Nepal Airlines flight, which also carried a 35-member team accompanying him for the engagements in Delhi.",
   "summary_zh": "订阅即可解锁。尼泊尔总理巴伦德拉·沙赫于2026年11月22日星期日下午抵达新德里，首次对印度进行正式访问。会谈后，贾伊尚卡尔先生表示：“很荣幸在尼泊尔总理巴伦·沙赫此次访问新德里期间于今晚拜会他。2026年11月22日星期日早些时候，沙赫先生乘坐尼泊尔航空公司航班离开加德满都，该航班还载有陪同他赴新德里参加各项活动的35人团队。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Account subscription benefits alongside Premium Stories, Editorials, Opinions and more. Unlock these with Subscription The Prime Minister of Nepal, Balendra Shah, arrived in New Delhi on Sunday (November 22, 2026) afternoon for his first official visit to India. Sources said that Mr. Shah will inaugurate several projects on Monday and is scheduled to hold talks with Prime Minister Narendra Modi. According to sources, Monday’s (November 23, 2026) discussion between the two Prime Ministers will give “political direction” to bilateral relations for the coming years. On Sunday (November 22, 2026), Mr. Shah was received at the airport by Jitin Prasada, the Minister of State for Commerce and Industry, Electronics and Information Technology. His first formal meeting of the visit took place in the evening, when External Affairs Minister S. Jaishankar called on him. After the meeting, Mr. Jaishankar said, “Privileged to call on PM Balen Shah of Nepal on his visit to New Delhi this evening. India cherishes the special friendship with Nepal. Look forward to his engagements with PM Narendra Modi tomorrow.” Mr. Shah, a rapper and former mayor of Kathmandu, took office as Nepal’s Prime Minister in March after his Rastriya Swatantra Party's (RSP’s) landslide victory in the elections to replace the interim government that was in place following the Gen Z uprising of September 2025. The RSP defeated older political parties like the Nepali Congress and the Maoists, who had dominated the country’s political landscape since the Constituent Assembly elections of 2008. Mr. Modi had invited Mr. Shah to India soon after the latter was sworn in as Prime Minister. The two leaders have interacted over the telephone and exchanged messages on social media as well as through diplomatic channels, but Monday (November 23, 2026) will be the first time they meet in person. The Hindu was told that the major agreements between the two sides are expected to be in the areas of development partnership, energy, hydropower, railways, connectivity, climate change, disaster resilience, infrastructure, and technology. On Saturday (November 21, 2026), The Hindu reported that the Dharchula Bridge, the land port of Banbasa at the India-Nepal border in Uttarakhand, and a train connection between Janakpur and Gorakhpur are expected to be inaugurated on Monday (November 23, 2026) by the two leaders. The two sides are in talks for new railway links between Raxaul and Kathmandu, which would open new freight and passenger connections. Earlier on Sunday (November 22, 2026), Mr. Shah left Kathmandu on a Nepal Airlines flight, which also carried a 35-member team accompanying him for the engagements in Delhi. Having introduced a no-frills administration, Mr. Shah did not have a ceremonial farewell at the Tribhuvan International Airport, as was the norm during the tenure of previous Prime Ministers of Nepal. Moving away from past tradition, the Nepal Embassy is also not likely to host Mr. Shah for a civic reception, as had been done during similar visits in the past. The business delegation from Nepal was hosted at an event organised by the Confederation of Indian Industry on Sunday (November 22, 2026) evening, which was attended by the country’s Finance Minister, Swarnim Wagley. Nepal's Foreign Minister, Shisir Khanal, is also accompanying Mr. Shah. Nepal’s Prime Minister will be given a ceremonial reception at the Rashtrapati Bhavan on Monday (November 23, 2026) morning, following which he will proceed to the memorial of Mahatma Gandhi at Rajghat. After this, he will take part in talks with Mr. Modi at Hyderabad House. Subsequently, Mr. Shah will call on President Droupadi Murmu in the afternoon before emplaning for Kathmandu. Comments have to be in English, and in full sentences. They cannot be abusive or personal. Please abide by our community guidelines for posting your comments. We have migrated to a new commenting platform. If you are already a registered user of The Hindu and logged in, you may continue to engage with our articles. If you do not have an account please register and login to post comments. Users can access their older comments by logging into their accounts on Vuukle",
