   "ageDays": 1.59,
   "summary": "The minister also reiterated the government’s commitment to a comprehensive, multi-dimensional strategy to prevent and counter terrorism, while calling for stronger intelligence, technological and operational partnerships with the European Union (EU) and regional allies.",
   "summary_zh": "这位部长还重申了政府致力于采取全面、多维度的战略来预防和打击恐怖主义，同时呼吁与欧洲联盟（EU）及区域盟友加强情报、技术和行动合作。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "The Federal Government has stated that lasting peace requires dismantling the criminal economies that finance insurgency, including kidnapping for ransom, illegal mining, cattle rustling and illicit arms trafficking. The minister also reiterated the government’s commitment to a comprehensive, multi-dimensional strategy to prevent and counter terrorism, while calling for stronger intelligence, technological and operational partnerships with the European Union (EU) and regional allies. General Musa further reaffirmed Nigeria’s commitment to collective regional security through the Multinational Joint Task Force (MNJTF) in the Lake Chad Basin, ECOWAS, the African Union (AU) and international initiatives such as the West Africa Police Information System (WAPIS). Outlining Nigeria’s counter-terrorism strategy under the leadership of President Bola Ahmed Tinubu, the minister noted that terrorism is a complex security challenge that exploits economic vulnerabilities, porous borders, local grievances and transnational organised crime. Addressing the evolving tactics of violent extremist groups, the minister highlighted Nigeria’s proactive measures to counter the illicit use of drones, digital communications and satellite technologies. “Through intelligence-led operations, advanced surveillance, unmanned aerial platforms and military artificial intelligence, the Armed Forces of Nigeria continue to degrade terrorist capabilities. “Notably, in May 2026, troops of Operation Hadin Kai successfully intercepted more than 400 Starlink communication devices linked to terrorist networks in the North-East,” the statement said. Beyond operational interceptions, Musa said the ministry is actively promoting indigenous defence innovation through research and private-sector partnerships, while seeking closer collaboration with the EU in counter-drone technologies, digital forensics and satellite intelligence. The minister stated that the Armed Forces of Nigeria remain strictly bound by national laws and international humanitarian law, prioritising civilian protection, due process in the prosecution of suspects, and structured rehabilitation and reintegration pathways for eligible former combatants through initiatives such as Operation SAFE CORRIDOR. The Schuman Security and Defence Forum provides a platform for high-level dialogue on international peace, security and defence issues. It brings together defence ministers from partner countries and EU Member States, representatives of international organisations and leading think tanks. Founded on January 22, 1995, THISDAY is published by THISDAY NEWSPAPERS LTD., 35 Creek Road Apapa, Lagos, Nigeria with offices in 36 states of Nigeria , the Federal Capital Territory and around the world. It is Nigeria’s most authoritative news media available on all platforms for the political, business, professional and diplomatic elite and broader middle classes while serving as the meeting point of new ideas, culture and technology for the aspirationals and millennials. The newspaper is a public trust dedicated to the pursuit of truth and reason covering a range of issues from breaking news to politics, business, the markets, the arts, sports and community to the crossroads of people and society. You can email us at: hello@thisdaylive.com or visit our contact us page",
